# MCP and agent access

The Uncoil Docs MCP server gives AI agents read-only access to every public Uncoil documentation chapter. It supports listing, searching, and reading Markdown documentation without exposing project data, API keys, traces, or dashboard actions.

## Install the remote server

Use the Streamable HTTP endpoint in an MCP client that supports remote servers:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "uncoil-docs": {
      "url": "https://www.uncoil.dev/api/docs/mcp"
    }
  }
}
```

The server exposes three read-only tools: `list_docs`, `search_docs`, and `read_doc`. It also exposes each document as a `uncoil://docs/<slug>` Markdown resource.

## Send a page to an AI chat

Each documentation page has a **Send to** menu. Choose **Copy Markdown**, **Send to ChatGPT**, or **Send to Claude**. The chat actions open a new conversation with the page text as context; review the content before sharing it with any third-party service.

The docs MCP server is for public documentation only. Project traces, prompts, evaluations, API keys, and other workspace data stay behind Uncoil authentication and are not available through this endpoint.
